<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Sometimes Fate is Wrong</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œNo,â€ Adora choked out, taking a step back as Horde Primeâ€™s smiling face began to take form where Catra had been. â€œNo, no, no!â€ Adora held her head in her hands as she stumbled back more. This couldnâ€™t be happening again. â€œYouâ€™re not real!â€ Tears begin to prick at the blondeâ€™s eyes. â€œYou...youâ€™re notâ€¦â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œAdora? Adora, are you okay?â€ The voice broke her from her panic, confusion now washing over her. The voice wasnâ€™t Catraâ€™s or Primeâ€™s. It was-&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora looked up to meet amethyst eyes and a now concerned look. Glimmer was now standing where Catra once had been, her hand outreached in the same gesture.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œGlim?â€ Adoraâ€™s voice was soft as she fixed her posture, her eyes not being able to look anywhere but the girl in front of her.&lt;br /&gt;â€œHey, â€˜Dora.â€ The girlâ€™s smile grew a bit. â€œYou okay?â€&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
